(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Distinguish between Centre of Gravity, Centre of Mass, and Centroid of an Area. State the mathematical definitions for each and specify under what physical conditions they coincide.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definitions and Physical Concepts:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Centre of Gravity \(CG\): The unique physical point in a body through which the resultant) Tj
T*
(   gravitational body force \(total weight W\) acts, regardless of the body's spatial orientation.) Tj
T*
(   Mathematically, it represents the first moment of gravitational force distribution:) Tj
T*
(   x_cg = Integral\(x dW\) / W = Integral\(x * g * dm\) / Integral\(g * dm\)) Tj
T*
(   y_cg = Integral\(y dW\) / W = Integral\(y * g * dm\) / Integral\(g * dm\)) Tj
T*
(   z_cg = Integral\(z dW\) / W = Integral\(z * g * dm\) / Integral\(g * dm\)) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Centre of Mass \(CM\): The point representing the mean spatial location of mass distribution.) Tj
T*
(   It is completely independent of external gravitational fields and governs translational) Tj
T*
(   dynamics:) Tj
T*
(   x_cm = Integral\(x dm\) / M = Integral\(x * rho * dV\) / Integral\(rho * dV\)) Tj
T*
(   y_cm = Integral\(y dm\) / M = Integral\(y * rho * dV\) / Integral\(rho * dV\)) Tj
T*
(   z_cm = Integral\(z dm\) / M = Integral\(z * rho * dV\) / Integral\(rho * dV\)) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Centroid: The purely geometric center of a geometric entity \(line, area, or volume\).) Tj
T*
(   For a 2D planar cross-section, it depends strictly on boundary geometry without mass density:) Tj
T*
(   x_bar = Integral\(x dA\) / A = Q_y / A) Tj
T*
(   y_bar = Integral\(y dA\) / A = Q_x / A) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Exact Conditions for Coincidence:) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 1 \(CM coincides with CG\): When the gravitational acceleration field 'g' is strictly) Tj
T*
(   uniform across the entire physical volume of the body \(g = constant\). This holds true for) Tj
T*
(   virtually all civil engineering terrestrial structures \(bridges, buildings, retaining walls\).) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 2 \(Centroid coincides with CM and CG\): When the material density rho is homogeneous) Tj
T*
(   and uniform throughout the entire cross-section or volume \(rho = constant\).) Tj
T*
(   Under uniform gravity and homogeneous material density, CG, CM, and Centroid are identical.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove both Theorems of Pappus-Guldinus for the determination of surface areas and volumes of bodies of revolution.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. First Theorem of Pappus-Guldinus \(Surface Area of Revolution\):) Tj
T*
(   Statement: The surface area A generated by revolving a plane curve of total length L about) Tj
T*
(   a non-intersecting coplanar axis equals the product of curve length L and the distance) Tj
T*
(   traversed by the curve's centroid during revolution.) Tj
T*
(   Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Let the axis of revolution be the x-axis. Consider an infinitesimal curve element of length dL) Tj
T*
(   located at distance y from the x-axis. When revolved through 2*pi radians, it generates an) Tj
T*
(   infinitesimal surface ring of area: dA = 2 * pi * y * dL.) Tj
T*
(   Integrating along the entire length L of the curve:) Tj
T*
(   Area = Integral\(dA\) = Integral\(2 * pi * y * dL\) = 2 * pi * Integral\(y dL\)) Tj
T*
(   By definition of the centroidal coordinate of a plane curve: y_bar = Integral\(y dL\) / L.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: Integral\(y dL\) = y_bar * L.) Tj
T*
(   Substituting gives the final theorem: Area = 2 * pi * y_bar * L. \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Second Theorem of Pappus-Guldinus \(Volume of Revolution\):) Tj
T*
(   Statement: The volume V generated by revolving a plane area A about a non-intersecting) Tj
T*
(   coplanar axis equals the product of plane area A and the distance traversed by its centroid.) Tj
T*
ET

