/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Let the axis of revolution be the x-axis. Consider a differential area element dA at distance) Tj
T*
(   y.) Tj
T*
(   Revolving dA through 2*pi radians sweeps out a circular ring of volume: dV = 2 * pi * y * dA.) Tj
T*
(   Integrating over the total plane area A:) Tj
T*
(   Volume = Integral\(dV\) = Integral\(2 * pi * y * dA\) = 2 * pi * Integral\(y dA\)) Tj
T*
(   By definition of the centroid of a plane area: y_bar = Integral\(y dA\) / A => Integral\(y dA\) =) Tj
T*
(   y_bar * A.) Tj
T*
(   Substituting yields: Volume = 2 * pi * y_bar * A. \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Critical Constraint:) Tj
T*
(   The axis of revolution must lie in the same plane as the generating figure and must NOT) Tj
T*
(   intersect the generating curve or area \(it may touch the boundary tangentially\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
