/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove the Parallel Axis Theorem \(Steiner's Theorem\) for area moments of inertia and explain why the reference axis must be centroidal.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of the Parallel Axis Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   The moment of inertia I of any plane area A about an arbitrary axis in its plane equals) Tj
T*
(   the moment of inertia I_G about a parallel centroidal axis passing through the centroid G,) Tj
T*
(   plus the product of the total area A and the square of the perpendicular distance d between the) Tj
T*
(   two axes:) Tj
T*
(   I = I_G + A * d^2) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation and Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Let G be the centroid of plane area A. Establish a centroidal coordinate system \(x', y'\)) Tj
T*
(   with origin at G. Consider a parallel target axis x located at perpendicular distance d below) Tj
T*
(   the x'-axis.) Tj
T*
(   The coordinate of any differential area element dA with respect to the target axis x is:) Tj
T*
(   y = y' + d) Tj
T*
(   By definition, the moment of inertia about the target x-axis is:) Tj
T*
(   I_x = Integral\(y^2 dA\) = Integral\( \(y' + d\)^2 dA \)) Tj
T*
(   Expanding the algebraic square:) Tj
T*
(   I_x = Integral\( \(y'^2 + 2*d*y' + d^2\) dA \)) Tj
T*
(   I_x = Integral\(y'^2 dA\) + 2*d * Integral\(y' dA\) + d^2 * Integral\(dA\)) Tj
T*
(   Evaluate each integral term independently:) Tj
T*
(   - Term 1: Integral\(y'^2 dA\) is by definition the centroidal moment of inertia I_Gx.) Tj
T*
(   - Term 2: Integral\(y' dA\) is the first moment of area about the centroidal x'-axis.) Tj
T*
(   Since x' passes through the centroid, Integral\(y' dA\) = A * y'_bar = A * 0 = 0!) Tj
T*
(   - Term 3: Integral\(dA\) is the total cross-sectional area A => d^2 * A = A * d^2.) Tj
T*
(   Substituting these evaluations:) Tj
T*
(   I_x = I_Gx + 0 + A * d^2 = I_Gx + A * d^2. \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Crucial Engineering Caveat:) Tj
T*
(   The theorem holds strictly when transferring between a CENTROIDAL axis and a parallel axis.) Tj
T*
(   To transfer between two non-centroidal parallel axes 1 and 2, one must first transfer from axis) Tj
T*
(   1) Tj
T*
(   back to the centroid \(I_G = I_1 - A*d1^2\), and then from centroid to axis 2 \(I_2 = I_G +) Tj
T*
(   A*d2^2\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
