12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A structural steel T-section has a top flange of 200 mm x 20 mm and a vertical web of 20 mm x 180 mm \(total depth 200 mm\). Determine: \(1\) Position of centroid from bottom base, \(2\) Centroidal moments of inertia I_xx and I_yy, \(3\) Radii of gyration k_xx and k_yy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Subdivision into Standard Geometric Elements:) Tj
T*
(   Due to symmetry about the vertical centerline of the web: x_bar = 0 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Divide into two rectangular components:) Tj
T*
(   - Flange 1 \(Top\): b1 = 200 mm, h1 = 20 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Area A1 = 200 * 20 = 4000 mm^2.) Tj
T*
(   Centroid y1 from bottom = 180 + \(20 / 2\) = 190.0 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Web 2 \(Bottom\): b2 = 20 mm, h2 = 180 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Area A2 = 20 * 180 = 3600 mm^2.) Tj
T*
(   Centroid y2 from bottom = 180 / 2 = 90.0 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Centroid Height y_bar:) Tj
T*
(   Total Area A = A1 + A2 = 4000 + 3600 = 7600 mm^2.) Tj
T*
(   Sigma\(Ai * yi\) = \(4000 * 190.0\) + \(3600 * 90.0\) = 760,000 + 324,000 = 1,084,000 mm^3.) Tj
T*
(   y_bar = Sigma\(Ai * yi\) / A = 1,084,000 / 7600 = 142.63 mm from bottom.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Centroidal Moment of Inertia I_xx \(Parallel Axis Theorem\):) Tj
T*
(   Distance from element centroids to neutral axis:) Tj
T*
(   d1 = |y1 - y_bar| = |190.0 - 142.63| = 47.37 mm.) Tj
T*
