(   [Problem Statement]: A symmetrical I-beam has top and bottom flanges of 200 mm x 20 mm and a vertical web of 10 mm x 260 mm \(overall depth 300 mm\). Calculate: \(1\) Centroidal I_xx, \(2\) Centroidal I_yy, \(3\) Section modulus Z_xx and Z_yy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometry and Symmetry Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Overall width B = 200 mm; Overall depth D = 300 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Flange width b_f = 200 mm, thickness t_f = 20 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Web thickness t_w = 10 mm, web height h_w = 300 - \(2 * 20\) = 260 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Due to double symmetry about both major x and minor y axes:) Tj
T*
(   Centroid G is at geometric center \(x_bar = 100 mm, y_bar = 150 mm from bottom\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Centroidal Moment of Inertia I_xx via Negative Subtraction Method:) Tj
T*
(   The I-section can be computed as a solid bounding rectangle minus two open void spaces:) Tj
T*
(   Bounding rectangle: B = 200 mm, D = 300 mm => I_box = \(200 * 300^3\) / 12 = 450.0 * 10^6 mm^4.) Tj
T*
(   Two void rectangles: width = \(200 - 10\) / 2 = 95 mm each, height = 260 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Combined void width b_void = 200 - 10 = 190 mm, height = 260 mm.) Tj
T*
(   I_voids = \(190 * 260^3\) / 12 = 278.29 * 10^6 mm^4.) Tj
T*
(   Total I_xx = I_box - I_voids = 450.0 * 10^6 - 278.29 * 10^6 = 171.71 * 10^6 mm^4.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Centroidal Moment of Inertia I_yy \(About Minor Axis\):) Tj
T*
(   - Top and bottom flanges \(2 flanges\): 2 * [ \(20 * 200^3\) / 12 ] = 2 * 13.333 * 10^6 = 26.67 *) Tj
T*
(   10^6 mm^4.) Tj
T*
(   - Web: \(260 * 10^3\) / 12 = 0.0217 * 10^6 mm^4.) Tj
T*
(   Total I_yy = 26.67 * 10^6 + 0.02 * 10^6 = 26.69 * 10^6 mm^4.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Section Moduli Z_xx and Z_yy:) Tj
T*
(   Extreme fiber distance from x-axis: y_max = D / 2 = 300 / 2 = 150 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Z_xx = I_xx / y_max = \(171.71 * 10^6 mm^4\) / 150 mm = 1,144,733 mm^3 = 1.145 * 10^6 mm^3.) Tj
T*
(   Extreme fiber distance from y-axis: x_max = B / 2 = 200 / 2 = 100 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Z_yy = I_yy / x_max = \(26.69 * 10^6 mm^4\) / 100 mm = 266,900 mm^3 = 0.267 * 10^6 mm^3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Engineering Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The beam is approximately 4.3 times stronger in bending resistance about its major axis \(Z_xx /) Tj
T*
(   Z_yy = 4.29\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
