12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive from first principles by direct integration the centroid and centroidal moment of inertia of a triangular area of base b and height h.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Coordinate System & Differential Strip Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   Consider a triangle of base b and vertical height h.) Tj
T*
(   Place the vertex \(apex\) at origin \(0, h\) and horizontal base of length b along the x-axis \(y =) Tj
T*
(   0\).) Tj
T*
(   Take a horizontal differential strip of thickness dy at distance y above the base.) Tj
T*
(   By similar triangles, width w\(y\) of the strip at height y is:) Tj
T*
(   w\(y\) / b = \(h - y\) / h => w\(y\) = b * \(1 - y / h\)) Tj
T*
(   Differential area of the strip: dA = w\(y\) dy = b * \(1 - y / h\) dy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Centroid Height y_bar from Base:) Tj
T*
(   Total area: A = Integral_0^h dA = Integral_0^h b * \(1 - y/h\) dy = b * [ y - y^2 / 2h ]_0^h = b) Tj
T*
(   * h / 2.) Tj
T*
(   First moment of area about base x-axis:) Tj
T*
(   Q_x = Integral_0^h y dA = Integral_0^h y * b * \(1 - y/h\) dy = b * Integral_0^h \(y - y^2 / h\) dy) Tj
T*
(   Q_x = b * [ y^2 / 2 - y^3 / 3h ]_0^h = b * [ h^2 / 2 - h^2 / 3 ] = b * h^2 / 6.) Tj
T*
(   Centroid coordinate:) Tj
T*
